+## Embedding it: triggers, aliases and scripts
+
+An app with its own script editor reads and changes a profile's triggers, aliases and scripts as the
+GUI's editor does, by `ScriptItemKind`, with no `dlgTriggerEditor`. Items are known by their ids, which
+a profile keeps while it runs; the temporary items scripts make, which the editor does not show, are
+left out of everything here.
+
+`scriptItems()` lists a kind's items depth first, each folder before what is in it, in the editor's
+order: each item's id, its folder's id (0 at the top level), name, whether it is a folder, `enabled`
+(switched on, as the editor's checkbox shows it), `active` (switched on, compiled and in folders that
+run), the package or module it came with, and `error`, why it cannot run, as plain text. It is a
+getter, so it may be called from any handler. `scriptItem()` gives all of one item's fields in a
+`QVariantMap`, by the names `editScriptItem()` takes: those, its Lua as `script`, and those of its kind:
+
+- a trigger's `patterns`, each a map of `text` and `type`, one of `substring`, `regex`, `startOfLine`,
+  `exact`, `lua`, `spacer` (its text the number of lines), `color` (its text as the profile keeps it,
+  as `ANSI_COLORS_F{1}_B{IGNORE}`) and `prompt`; `command`; `lineDelta`, the lines a multi-line
+  trigger's patterns may be spread over, -1 for a trigger of one line, as the editor shows it;
+  `matchAll`, `filter`, `fireLength` (the lines it stays open for), `sound`, `soundFile`,
+  `highlight`, and `highlightFg` and `highlightBg` as `#rrggbb`, or empty to keep the text's colour;
+- an alias's `pattern` and `command`;
+- a script's `eventHandlers`, a list of event names.
+
+`addScriptItem()` makes an item or a folder as the editor's add does: switched on, but not running
+until its first `editScriptItem()`, at a place among the items the editor shows in that folder.
+`editScriptItem()` sets the fields it is given and keeps the rest, then saves the item as the editor's
+save does: the name trimmed, its patterns and Lua compiled, a new item set running if that worked
+(but not during the emergency stop, which starts it as it ends) and a trigger that did not compile
+stopped and switched off, with its error kept for `scriptItem()` to give, which the call is still
+true for. Saving a script runs it, as in the GUI. An alias given no name takes its pattern, and one
+whose replacement matches its own pattern is refused, as it would call itself forever.
+`setScriptItemEnabled()` switches an item on or off as the editor's checkbox does, leaving off one
+that does not compile; `moveScriptItem()` moves one into a folder or to the top level, as a drag in
+the editor does, and refuses a folder into itself; `deleteScriptItem()` deletes one, and all in it.
+Each write is false, with the reason in `errorString()` and nothing changed, where `submit()` is
+refused, while a trigger, alias or event handler runs (as one does that waits on the event loop),
+for an id not of that kind, a parent that is not a folder, a field not of that kind or a value of the
+wrong type. What they change is written with the profile's next save, as the GUI's editor's is.
+
